  "dominant_obstruction": "Every homogeneous static relation lies in the orthogonal complement of the nonzero factor-base log vector, so even a free maximal kernel has rank only 163 and leaves one scale. Unanchored decompositions of a fixed target likewise determine only the projective class of (ell,d). Starting from maximal static rank, one generator-anchored row still leaves one unknown and two independent anchored rows are necessary. The registered free one-anchor boundary is already 1.446505 times rho, and no non-scalar-labelled two-row event is constructed.",
  "decision": "Reject static homogeneous factor-base structure as a complete logarithm quotient. Credit at most rank K-1, require two independently replayable generator-anchored rows after that quotient, and charge their discovery and full recovery pipeline. Keep a structured two-row anchored event open; do not attempt an unplanted full-depth relation.",
